; Purity has one spelling, `;@axiom:effect(pure)`, like every other
; effect claim. `;@axiom:pure` and any slip of it - `pur`, `PURE` - are
; AX3078 wherever they stand, a function or a `data` declaration alike.
; `pre` is one letter from `pure` too, and is a key the compiler checks,
; so it draws nothing; `effect(pure)` is the control.
;@axiom:pure
(:: bare (-> Int Int))
(fn (bare n)
  n)

;@axiom:pur
(:: slipped (-> Int Int))
(fn (slipped n)
  n)

;@axiom:PURE
(data Reading
  (Reading Int))

;@axiom:pre((> n 0))
(:: guarded (-> Int Int))
(fn (guarded n)
  n)

;@axiom:effect(pure)
(:: control (-> Int Int))
(fn (control n)
  n)

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  0)
